WEBVTT

NOTE Recording started 2026-09-15 10:02 IST

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.120
<v Alice Fernandes>Right, let's start. Two things today: the login problems and how we handle releases.</v>

2
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:15.880
<v Bob Mehta>Support sent over six tickets this week from people who cannot get back into their accounts after forgetting their password.</v>

3
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:24.300
<v Alice Fernandes>Yes, we still have no password reset flow. I will build the email based reset flow, I can have it ready by Friday.</v>

4
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:31.050
<v Carol D'Souza>Careful, I think something like that was already filed a while back. Worth checking before you open a new ticket.</v>

5
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:39.900
<v Bob Mehta>Separate thing, the login endpoint has no rate limiting at all. Somebody hit it two thousand times last night.</v>

6
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:47.600
<v Alice Fernandes>That is urgent, it is open to anyone. Bob, can you add rate limiting on that endpoint this week?</v>

7
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:52.400
<v Bob Mehta>Sure, I will do it by Wednesday.</v>

8
00:00:52.800 --> 00:01:02.200
<v Carol D'Souza>The reports page is also timing out. Three endpoints take over ten seconds because of missing indexes. I will look into the slow queries.</v>

9
00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:09.400
<v Dave Patil>At some point it would be nice to have dark mode as well. Not urgent, just something people keep asking about.</v>

10
00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:14.100
<v Alice Fernandes>Let's park dark mode for now, nobody has time for it this sprint.</v>

11
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:23.800
<v Eve Sharma>On releases, shipping whenever we feel like it is not working. I suggest we release every Thursday afternoon and freeze changes on Thursday morning.</v>

12
00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:29.700
<v Alice Fernandes>Agreed, weekly release on Thursday it is. Everyone okay with that?</v>

13
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.200
<v Carol D'Souza>Works for me.</v>

14
00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:41.900
<v Dave Patil>Also we decided last month to move the database to Postgres, and that migration is still half done. I am on it, but it will take another two weeks.</v>

15
00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:50.600
<v Eve Sharma>One more thing, the setup steps in our onboarding doc are out of date. The new joiner lost a full day on it. I will update the onboarding guide.</v>

16
00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:57.300
<v Alice Fernandes>Thanks Eve. That is everything, let's pick this up again in next week's planning.</v>
